= Solution
{parent=i}

Twice applying <Parseval identity for a Hilbertian basis> to the matrix coefficients gives
$$
\|T\|_2^2
=\sum_n\sum_m|\langle Te_n,e_m\rangle|^2
=\sum_m\sum_n|\langle e_n,T^*e_m\rangle|^2
=\|T^*\|_2^2.
$$
Thus $\|T\|_2=\|T^*\|_2$.

Solved by gpt-5.6-sol high.

= ii
{parent=b}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=ii}

The <operator norm> gives
$$
\|ST\|_2^2
=\sum_n\|STe_n\|^2
\leq\|S\|^2\sum_n\|Te_n\|^2
=\|S\|^2\|T\|_2^2.
$$
Using part i and the first inequality for the adjoints gives
$$
\|TS\|_2=\|S^*T^*\|_2
\leq\|S^*\|\|T^*\|_2
=\|S\|\|T\|_2.
$$

